{"kind":"panel","id":"597ad792-4af7-48f4-a5f7-3f35a5568ef2","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"The River","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[0,-300,520,220],"src":[],"text":"The River - lesson 1 of the Alpaca4d Playground.\n\nA C24 timber plank, 300 x 50 mm, across a 4 m river: a pin at one end, a roller at the other, and the alpaca, 0.6 kN, standing in the middle.\n\nCheck it by hand: PL^3 / 48EI = 0.6 x 4^3 / (48 x 10 500 000 x 0.3 x 0.05^3 / 12) = 24.4 mm. Model View draws it eight times bigger.\n\nTry: stand the plank on its edge (swap Plank width and Plank thickness), or wire Free into nothing, so that both ends are built in.","colour":[0,0,0,0]}
